{"assets":["/editorial-assets/b411eec4c32b4baa24a73fc34390046d5d2ffc5c0aaf0fbca4b310e88d8d01c8.png","/editorial-assets/6b02b9974ccd0e4fbddd9141631b2a5756f72eb25085782aa45fc305c16c699b.png"],"contestId":"215","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hi! I'll try to explain solution of problem E on Codeforces Round #132."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ok, in the very beginning let's try solve some other task. We'll find the number of such integers in the interval (2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"], where "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b411eec4c32b4baa24a73fc34390046d5d2ffc5c0aaf0fbca4b310e88d8d01c8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". And someone can see that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" has length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we should try blocks of {0, 1} to be the same part of periodical number. These blocks have length, which is divisor of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's calculate number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] of such blocks of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is some divisor of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of first(from the left side) bits of number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and name it as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" >> ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), e.g. if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 10011000"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 4 then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1001"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2 then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Firstly, we should check block "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", it needs for example to check number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ttttt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"... repeated "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/6b02b9974ccd0e4fbddd9141631b2a5756f72eb25085782aa45fc305c16c699b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" times, it can be calculated in a loop "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" << "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". It's clear if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we should take into account this block "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = 1. It's clear that every correct block less or equal than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and it should begin from 1 (because of periodical number is without leading zeroes). Case of equality we took. And we should add to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] difference between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 10000..."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" i-1 zeroes, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - (1 << ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1)). It seems that all is ready and we can sum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] for every divisor of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and not equal "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", but we cant. Because some cases we count more than once, e.g. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 10101100"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 4, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[4] = 1 + (1010"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1000"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") = 3 we considered cases of blocks 1000, 1001, 1010, and when we count for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2,"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[2] = 1 + (10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") = 1, we considered one case 10, but 1010 is obtained from 10 repeated two times. But we can easily escape these problems, for this we should substract from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" divides "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Some note. We get some DP problem, we calculate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1 to the most divisor of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" which is not equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and update its value by substracting all g[j]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us summarize some ideas, we can count number of periodical numbers in the interval (2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"], by going through divisors of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and calculating "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"], and then we return sum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"g"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" divides "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". One can see that 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" cant be periodical. Given this fact we will calculate this value for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, then 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 and so on.In the end we get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1, and we get set of non-intersecting intervals, counting on each of them and sum up it we get answer. It can be done recursively. My "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://ideone.com/96ZjG"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"code"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++, when I also precalculated divisors of each number from 1 to 60. I'm waiting for your replies and some criticism. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/5034"}